{"lap":31,"text":"Hill had pulled out a twenty-second lead ahead of Clark, but on the thirtieth lap he made contact with Jackie Lewis' Cooper when lapping him, allowing Clark to pass.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":8},{"lap":34,"text":"Hill gave chase, netting the lap record, and re-took the lead on lap 33.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":8},{"lap":42,"text":"Hill and BRM looked sure to win, but on lap 42 he retired in the hairpin with fuel injection and throttle linkage troubles; he lost several laps and ended up in last place after also having stopped in the hairpin to pick up the engine cover that he had left behind during his earlier visit there.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":8},{"lap":42,"text":"All of a sudden Gurney found himself in the lead, he made no mistakes and gained what was to be Porsche's only Grand Prix victory with their own car.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0},{"lap":49,"text":"His troubles were not over, however, with five laps left his throttle wire snapped and he had to control it with his hand - rather troublesome since his BRM's gear shifter was also on the right hand side.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":2}],"x":{"drivers":[],"cars":[{"id":"cooper_1962","ref":"cooper","name":"Cooper","year":1962,"pace":-1.678,"pace_sd":0.5,"deg_rel":0.0,"n_races":9,"p_mech_lap":0.0064,"colours":null,"source":"history"}]}}